<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<workout_file>
    <author>Domestique Library</author>
    <name>Anaerobic 2min descending-power ladder 5x (48min)</name>
    <description>Warmup: 5min ramp from 45% to 75% FTP, 3 x 30s fast-pedal drill @ 82%, primer 1min @ 88% + 1min @ 102% | Descending power at constant rung length: 2min @ 132%, 2min @ 126%, 2min @ 120%, 2min @ 114%, 2min @ 108% FTP, recoveries 5min 30s / 5min / 4min 45s / 4min 15s @ 45% | The rung length never changes, so the target is the only thing that moves - and it moves down. Ride each rung to its number and no harder: the anaerobic deficit carried out of the opening rungs is what makes 108% cost near the end what 132% cost fresh | Cooldown: 5min from 65% to 45% FTP</description>
    <sportType>bike</sportType>
    <workout>
        <Warmup Duration="300" PowerLow="0.45" PowerHigh="0.75" pace="0" />
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="0.82" pace="0" Cadence="110" />
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="0.45" pace="0" Cadence="85" />
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="0.82" pace="0" Cadence="110" />
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="0.45" pace="0" Cadence="85" />
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="0.82" pace="0" Cadence="110" />
        <SteadyState Duration="30" Power="0.45" pace="0" Cadence="85" />
